The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Shirley Ballas]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]].

==Professional dancers ==
On 6 March 2020, [[Kevin Clifton]] announced he was leaving the show after seven years.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a31259464/strictly-come-dancing-professional-kevin-clifton-leaves-quit/|title=Strictly Come Dancing professional Kevin Clifton leaves the show|last=Earp|first=Catherine|date=6 March 2020|website=Digital Spy|language=en-GB|access-date=6 March 2020}}</ref> Despite being confirmed in the 2020 professional line-up, on 26 March 2020, [[AJ Pritchard]] announced he was leaving the show after four years.<ref>{{cite news|last=Daly|first=Helen|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2020-03-26/strictly-come-dancing-aj-pritchard-quit/|title=AJ Pritchard quits BBC show – here's why|publisher=Radio Times|date=26 March 2020|access-date=28 March 2020}}</ref> The other professional dancers from 2019 were all confirmed to be returning for the series.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/355f2acd-1c2a-438f-a0a8-f75245114f91|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Pro-dancer line-up for 2020 revealed!|publisher=[[BBC One]]|date=12 March 2020|access-date=28 August 2020}}</ref> [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]] and [[Nadiya Bychkova]] only featured in group dances after having partners the previous year, alongside [[Graziano Di Prima]] and [[Nancy Xu]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Strictly Come Dancing's Neil Jones benched as pros without partners confirmed|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2020-09-28/strictly-come-dancing-2020-neil-jones-partner/|access-date=28 September 2020|website=Radio Times|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Strictly Come Dancing bosses 'recruit BGT star as part of pro dancers for 2020 series'|url=https://www.entertainmentdaily.co.uk/tv/strictly-come-dancing-bosses-recruit-bgt-star-as-part-of-pro-dancers-for-2020-series/|date=19 August 2020|access-date=25 October 2020|website=Entertainment Daily|last=Carter|first=Rebecca|language=en}}</ref>

Due to the pandemic, several changes had to be made in how the professional dancers performed. Firstly, the dancers had to shield at home for two weeks. They then formed a bubble which allowed them to stay in a hotel, where they could practise their routines. All of the group dances were pre-recorded.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/tv/tv-news/inside-strictly-come-dancings-luxury-22867560|title=Inside Strictly Come Dancing's luxury hotel where pros isolated and rehearsed in dance tent|work=[[Daily Mirror]]|first=Lewis|last=Knight|date=19 October 2020|access-date=23 October 2020|language=en-GB}}</ref>

==Couples==
This series featured twelve celebrity contestants. On 1 September 2020, the first three celebrities announced were [[Caroline Quentin]], [[Jason Bell (American football)|Jason Bell]], and [[Max George]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/175048bc-6060-4a91-8ffa-66f095c8e478|title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Meet our first three celebrities for Strictly 2020!|website=BBC One|date=1 September 2020|access-date=1 September 2020|language=en}}</ref> On 2 September 2020, it was announced that Olympic boxer [[Nicola Adams]] would be part of the first same-sex partnership.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-53989693?intlink_from_url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment_and_arts&link_location=live-reporting-story|title=Strictly Come Dancing: Ex-boxer Nicola Adams to have same-sex dance partner|publisher=[[BBC News]]|date=2 September 2020|access-date=2 September 2020|language=en}}</ref> On 3 September 2020, ''[[Made in Chelsea]]'' star [[Jamie Laing]] was confirmed to be participating in the series after having to withdraw from the [[Strictly Come Dancing (series 17)|seventeenth series]] due to a foot injury.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2020-09-03/jamie-laing-strictly-come-dancing-2020-contestant/|title=Meet Jamie Laing – Strictly Come Dancing 2020 contestant and Made in Chelsea Star|work=[[Radio Times]]|first=Grace|last=Henry|date=3 September 2020|access-date=6 September 2020|language=en}}</ref> Celebrity reveals continued throughout the week until the full line-up was revealed on 4 September 2020.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bt.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-2020-cast-lineup-celebrities|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2020: All the confirmed celebrities – The full list|publisher=[[BT TV]]|first=Alex|last=Fletcher|date=4 September 2020|access-date=6 September 2020|language=en}}</ref> On 12 November 2020, it was announced that [[Katya Jones]] had tested positive for [[Coronavirus disease 2019|COVID-19]], which meant that she and Nicola Adams had to withdraw from the competition due to the government's guidelines on self-isolation.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/6fdf823a-2afa-4803-8a33-a190b3af4019|title=Nicola and Katya leave Strictly 2020|publisher=[[BBC One]]|date=12 November 2020|access-date=12 November 2020|language=en-GB}}</ref>

